gorgias-polus.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P3 (S34): "disgraceful" is taken as more shameful in common opinion, as "you and the world" agree, i.e. worse in repute in P3 and as more shameful by the standard just agreed, i.e. exceeding in pain or evil (S11, S15) where more_disgraceful is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S20) does not follow (gorgias-polus.logic.r2.sense1)
gorgias-polus.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C1 (S20): more_disgraceful = F, more_disgraceful_2 = T, more_evil = F, more_painful = F
